Alright — here’s a solid list of MySQL interview questions (both beginner-friendly and tricky ones) that often come up, grouped by topic.

1. Basic SELECT & Filtering

	Get all employees whose salary is greater than 50000.

	Retrieve the top 3 highest salaries.

	Find employees who joined in the last 6 months.

	Select employees whose name starts with “A” and ends with “n”.

	Find employees whose manager_id is NULL.

2. Aggregations & Grouping

	Find the average salary in each department.

	Count the number of employees for each designation.

	Find departments having more than 5 employees.

	Get the salary that is received by more than one employee (HAVING COUNT(*) > 1).

	Find the highest paid employee in each department.

3. Joins

	Get employee name with their manager’s name (SELF JOIN).

	List employees along with department name (INNER JOIN).

	Show all employees and departments even if not assigned (LEFT JOIN).

	Find employees who do not have a manager (LEFT JOIN ... WHERE manager_id IS NULL).

4. Subqueries

	Find employees whose salary is above the average salary.

	Find the second highest salary (LIMIT/OFFSET or MAX inside subquery).

	Update all employees whose salary equals the maximum salary (the FROM clause trick we just discussed).

	Delete employees earning the minimum salary.

5. String & Date Functions

	Extract year from joining_date.

	Show employees whose email domain is "gmail.com".

	Find the difference in days between joining date and today.

	Convert names to uppercase.

6. Advanced / Tricky

	Self-join to get employee-manager hierarchy.

	Find Nth highest salary without using LIMIT.

	Find employees with duplicate email addresses.

	Find the department with the highest total salary (excluding managers).

	Write a query to pivot data (convert rows to columns).

	Explain the difference between:

	INNER JOIN vs LEFT JOIN

	UNION vs UNION ALL

	EXISTS vs IN

	Explain how indexing works and when to use it.

	Explain why UPDATE ... WHERE col = (SELECT ...) can throw error 1093.

7. Query Optimization / EXPLAIN

	How to check execution plan using EXPLAIN.

	How to detect slow queries in MySQL.

	Difference between clustered and non-clustered indexes in MySQL.

	How composite indexes work (INDEX(col1, col2)).

	Why LIKE '%abc' is slow and how to optimize.
